FINAL:
Built `/home/ubuntu/workspace/index.html` — a single self-contained page, no external assets.

**Features**
- **Add**: text input + Add button, Enter submits, trims whitespace and rejects empty tasks
- **Complete**: checkbox toggles done state with strikethrough styling
- **Delete**: per-item Delete button
- **Persistence**: whole list saved to `localStorage` under key `todo.items.v1`, reloaded and validated on startup; corrupt/blocked storage falls back to an empty in-memory list
- Also shows a remaining/total counter and a "Clear completed" action

**Verification (read back from disk)**
- 295 lines, 7,033 bytes; starts with `<!DOCTYPE html>`, ends with `</html>`
- All six `getElementById` targets exist (`list`, `empty`, `count`, `add-form`, `new-todo`, `clear-done`)
- `localStorage.getItem`/`setItem` plus `JSON.parse`/`JSON.stringify` present
- No `innerHTML` (item text is set via `textContent`, so stored text can't inject markup), no `src`/`href` references, `<script>`/`<style>` tags balanced
- JS bracket balance checked after stripping strings/comments: no mismatches

**Limitation**: no browser or process-execution tool is enabled in this session, so I could not click through the UI at runtime. Verification was static plus full read-back of the file; the add/toggle/delete logic is straightforward DOM code but was not executed in a browser.
